WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
- Can you explain to everybody
how you got the role?

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.800
- Yeah, I sent Baz a tape.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.120
I heard that he was making the film.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.850
I sent him a tape of me
singing "Unchained Melody",

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:09.900
and playing the piano.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.010
- God, I love that song.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.090
- [Austin] It's such a beautiful song.

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:13.650
- Classic.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:14.700
- And he responded to it.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.263
And then I flew to New York,

00:00:17.263 --> 00:00:19.611
and we met, and we just
talked for three hours,

00:00:19.611 --> 00:00:23.040
and then he said you
wanna come in tomorrow,

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.720
and read a couple scenes from the script?

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.940
And so I came in and read a couple scenes,

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.890
and then he said you
wanna come in tomorrow,

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:31.350
and read and sing a couple songs,

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.940
and you wanna sing "Suspicious Minds".

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.630
And so I went home that night, practiced,

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.170
and I come back, we ended up
doing that for five months.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.413
It was unlike any audition,

00:00:39.413 --> 00:00:41.370
where it was five months of exploring.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.350
- That's a relationship.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.183
- Yeah
- Yeah.

00:00:44.183 --> 00:00:47.426
- Completely, and then it
came time for the screen test,

00:00:47.426 --> 00:00:48.660
which...

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:50.190
- Then it came time for the?

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.023
Okay.

00:00:51.023 --> 00:00:52.320
- Because you know there comes a point

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.660
where the studio has to sign off.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.130
And there, you gotta do the screen test.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.499
And so I'd prepared everything,

00:00:58.499 --> 00:01:00.196
and got to the screen test,

00:01:00.196 --> 00:01:03.213
and Baz changed everything
on me on the day.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:06.300
I was supposed to do a couple scenes,

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.010
and he changed the scenes,

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:10.320
and changed all the words in the scenes.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.600
And then I was supposed
to sing three songs.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.720
He said, and then he starts
describing the scene to me.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.700
And he's saying, you're
gonna sing these three songs,

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.800
and they weren't the
songs that I prepared.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:21.450
And so suddenly I'm on set.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.640
and I go Baz I don't
think I have the material

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:24.660
that you gave me.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:25.770
And he goes, oh no, we changed it,

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:28.350
but I'll get you new material.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:30.720
And then turns out he never
got me a new material,

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:33.780
and he starts filming while
I'm learning everything.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:35.820
So then I started going through it,

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:37.200
and then he cut one of the scenes,

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.337
and he said now we're
gonna do you performing

00:01:39.337 --> 00:01:40.170
"Suspicious Minds".

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:43.347
- Is he just like messing
with you at this point?

00:01:43.347 --> 00:01:44.180
- I realize now...

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:46.140
- I would look around for
Ashton Kutcher at this point.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.280
Like, am I being punked?

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.640
- Being punked, yeah.
- That's horrible.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.750
- He put me through the ringer,

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:53.490
and I realize now it's 'cause that's,

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:56.040
he likes to be very spontaneous on set.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.320
He wanted to see if I would lose my mind.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.270
And so I didn't think I got it.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.100
And then a week later I got a call,

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.350
and I woke up to Baz calling me,

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:05.370
and I thought, okay

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:07.200
this is a moment I either
have it or I don't.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.700
And he's very dramatic in the
way that he goes about things.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.570
And so he sounded kind of downcast

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:13.472
and he goes
- Oh, how mean!

00:02:13.472 --> 00:02:17.190
- I just wanted to be the
first one to call you and say,

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:19.260
are you ready to fly Mr. Presley?

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:20.513
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:20.513 --> 00:02:21.420
- It was just the greatest
phone call I've ever had.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:22.253
- I love that.

